    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0538" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/3170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Walton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-04T17:00:00-04:00">September 4, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50 [bis]. Your 80, September 2, 10 a.m., first paragraph. The Department desires
                    that you ascertain by thorough investigation whether the practices referred to
                    in your despatch no. 646<anchor n="12" xml:id="d553-f1"/> have actually been
                    discontinued. If any such practices still exist, you should submit by mail full
                    particulars, including names of parties involved.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d553-f2"
                    /> The Department also desires specific information in support of your statement
                    that the British Legation is refusing to grant export permits for shipments of
                    piassava from Liberia to the United States while granting permits for shipments
                    to England.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d553-f1" n="12" xml:id="d553-f1-content">
                <p>Dated July 10, <ref target="#pg527">p. 527</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d553-f2" n="13" xml:id="d553-f2-content">
                <p>In despatch No. 665, September 17, the Minister in Liberia reported that a
                    thorough investigation on this subject was not productive of tangible results
                    (740.00112 European War 1939/3667).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
